---
# ansible-lint config for home-iac's ansible/ tree.
#
# ugreen-nas-compose (the repo these roles were migrated from — see
# docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-21-netbox-udm-sync.md Task 1) never wired
# up ansible-lint at all (no pre-commit hook, no CI job, not even in its
# dev dependency group) — there is no upstream config to "match" here.
# This is a fresh addition, scoped to keep Task 1 a pure migration: no
# `profile:` tier is set (default/least-strict rule set) so this doesn't
# force rewrites of code that's supposed to be verbatim, no changes yet.
# Tighten the profile in a follow-up once the NetBox rewrite (Task 3+)
# touches this code anyway.

exclude_paths:
  - environments/ # OpenTofu, not Ansible
  - modules/ # OpenTofu, not Ansible
  - .cache/

# Demoted to warnings rather than fixed, because fixing them means editing
# the migrated roles — which Task 1 deliberately does NOT do (Step 1: "no
# changes yet"). All three are pre-existing, consistent stylistic choices
# in the ugreen-nas-compose originals, not accidental:
#   - var-naming[no-role-prefix]: every migrated role uses a short internal
#     `_<scope>_*` prefix (e.g. `_udm_dns_*`) for set_fact/register vars
#     instead of the full role-name prefix — consistent across all seven
#     roles, so this is a deliberate convention, not drift.
#   - yaml[line-length]: a handful of Jinja-heavy lines exceed 160 chars.
#   - name[template]: one task name embeds a Jinja expr mid-sentence.
# Revisit when Task 3 (rewriting unifi_network_dns_record) actually touches
# these files for a reason other than the move itself.
#
# Two more added for the JetKVM migration (home-iac#24, same "verbatim,
# no changes yet" rule), both in playbooks/jetkvm-netbird-update.yml and
# both already justified by an inline comment in the file predating the
# move — not accidental, and fixing either would undo a documented live
# finding:
#   - risky-shell-pipe: the checksum-verify task's `grep | cut` pipeline
#     deliberately skips `set -o pipefail` (see the task's own comment —
#     pinning /bin/bash for pipefail broke the play on NixOS control
#     nodes, where /bin holds only /bin/sh; the empty-`expected` check
#     already catches the failure pipefail would have caught).
#   - command-instead-of-module: the extract task uses plain `tar`, not
#     `ansible.builtin.unarchive`, because `unarchive` requires GNU tar
#     and refuses macOS bsdtar (also a live finding, per the task's
#     comment).
warn_list:
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
  - yaml[line-length]
  - name[template]
  - risky-shell-pipe
  - command-instead-of-module
